.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS " None pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.wheel\&.check_compatibility (Tuple[int, \&.\&.\&.] version, str name)"

.PP
.nf
Raises errors or warns if called with an incompatible Wheel-Version\&.

pip should refuse to install a Wheel-Version that's a major series
ahead of what it's compatible with (e\&.g 2\&.0 > 1\&.1); and warn when
installing a version only minor version ahead (e\&.g 1\&.2 > 1\&.1)\&.

version: a 2-tuple representing a Wheel-Version (Major, Minor)
name: name of wheel or package to raise exception about

:raises UnsupportedWheel: when an incompatible Wheel-Version is given

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Tuple[str, Message] pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.wheel\&.parse_wheel (ZipFile wheel_zip, str name)"

.PP
.nf
Extract information from the provided wheel, ensuring it meets basic
standards\&.

Returns the name of the \&.dist-info directory and the parsed WHEEL metadata\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " bytes pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.wheel\&.read_wheel_metadata_file (ZipFile source, str path)"

.SS " str pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.wheel\&.wheel_dist_info_dir (ZipFile source, str name)"

.PP
.nf
Returns the name of the contained \&.dist-info directory\&.

Raises AssertionError or UnsupportedWheel if not found, >1 found, or
it doesn't match the provided name\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Message pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.wheel\&.wheel_metadata (ZipFile source, str dist_info_dir)"

.PP
.nf
Return the WHEEL metadata of an extracted wheel, if possible\&.
Otherwise, raise UnsupportedWheel\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Tuple[int, \&.\&.\&.] pip\&._internal\&.utils\&.wheel\&.wheel_version (Message wheel_data)"

.PP
.nf
Given WHEEL metadata, return the parsed Wheel-Version\&.
Otherwise, raise UnsupportedWheel\&.

.fi
.PP
 
